@startuml use-cases
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' Challenge PHP Hexagonal - Use case diagram
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam actorStyle awesome

actor "API client\n(unauthenticated)" as Guest
actor "Authenticated user" as User
actor "GIPHY" as Giphy <<external system>>
actor "Audit trail" as Audit <<supporting system>>

rectangle "GIFs API" {
  usecase "UC1 - Login\n(email + password -> OAuth2 token, 30 min)" as UC1
  usecase "UC2 - Search GIFs\n(query, limit?, offset?)" as UC2
  usecase "UC3 - Get GIF by id" as UC3
  usecase "UC4 - Save favorite GIF\n(gif_id, alias, user_id)" as UC4
  usecase "UC5 - Record service interaction" as UC5
}

Guest --> UC1
User --> UC2
User --> UC3
User --> UC4

UC2 ..> Giphy : <<uses>>
UC3 ..> Giphy : <<uses>>
UC4 ..> UC3 : <<include>>\nthe gif must exist

UC1 ..> UC5 : <<include>>
UC2 ..> UC5 : <<include>>
UC3 ..> UC5 : <<include>>
UC4 ..> UC5 : <<include>>
UC5 --> Audit

note bottom of UC1
  The issued token is required by
  UC2, UC3 and UC4 (Authorization: Bearer).
end note

note right of UC4
  A user can only save favorites
  for themselves: user_id must match
  the authenticated identity.
end note
@enduml
